      "notes": "Your phase 4a note: 'not like a flute at all, more like a plucked laser gun'. That clip's laser was a vowel jump on every tongued note, which the profile no longer has; this is the articulator's flute, never heard before. Measured: the monk is buzzy where a flute is nearly a pure tone, because its third formant (2.2-2.9 kHz) lifts whichever harmonic meets it, sometimes above the note itself. 'No F3' switches that formant off (new helper key). 'Less breath' turns down the breath partials (3.8 and 5 kHz). 'Legato' glides quickly through slurred notes instead of tonguing each one. The melody is written around B5 and sung an octave lower (your D37 fold). Every clip at Gervill's loudness; blind mode is worth it.",
